        "lineage": "",
        "abstract": "The Scottish Public Sector LiDAR (Phase 4) was initially captured by Fugro for Scottish Power Energy Network (SPEN) from 2017 to 2019 to monitor their overhead power cable network under their Virtual World Asset Management programme. The Scottish Government procured this dataset for public use in 2020. This dataset covers total 17,945 square kilometres (note the dataset does not have full national coverage). This dataset reflects the LAS point cloud data with a density of 4ppm (points per square metre).",
